## Finding and bounded BUILD path

The accepted five-minute current-source reproduction still fails AC-4's maximum-gap condition: 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 seconds, mean 20.000523 fps, maximum EOF gap 89.163715 ms, and 753 of 6,049 gaps above 60 ms. The A/B/ABBA output-flush diagnostics found no repeatable benefit from `-flush_packets 1`; keep the production argv unchanged. The surviving medium-confidence localization is after V4L2 dequeue and before raw-pipe delivery inside FFmpeg processing/output. Python reader backlog, CPU runqueue delay as the primary cause, and sustained pipe backpressure remain unsupported; the internal wait/compute phase remains unknown. PTS are V4L2 SOE, not EOF; preserve `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time sampled after complete raw-frame read.

The approved next diagnostic is one read-only 600-frame capture using the default production argv on `/dev/video60`: correlate per-thread FFmpeg syscall timestamps/durations for `ioctl`, `futex`, `poll`/`ppoll`, `select`/`pselect6`, `epoll_wait`, and `read`/`readv`/`write`/`writev` with monotonic full-read completions and per-thread schedstat runtime/runqueue deltas. Keep the existing mode, one FFmpeg thread, one filter thread, queue size 1, reader, and all argv fixed. Use `strace -f -ttt -T`; keep payload arguments raw-only and save no frame bytes. For every >60 ms interval, report overlap with blocking syscall waits and per-thread runtime/runqueue deltas. A long syscall wait supports blocking; runtime without a blocking call is suggestive but does not prove CPU work; a scheduler delta supports runnable delay. Strace and post-read `/proc` snapshots add observer overhead. This is diagnostic only, not an AC-4 pass or product fix.

